# DW Gold Trading Beginner Questions

## What is a stop loss?
A stop loss is your safety line. If the trade goes the wrong way, it closes the trade at a set level to help protect your account.

## What is take profit?
Take profit is your target. It closes the trade automatically if price reaches the level you chose.

## What is spread?
Spread is the gap between the buy price and sell price. A bigger spread means the trade starts more expensive.

## What is lot size?
Lot size is how big the trade is. Bigger lot size means bigger wins and bigger losses. Beginners should keep lot size small while learning.

## What is leverage?
Leverage lets you control a bigger trade with less money, but it also makes losses bigger. It must be used carefully.

## What is margin?
Margin is money locked by the broker to keep a trade open.

## What is free margin?
Free margin is the money still available in the account after open trades are using margin.

## What is drawdown?
Drawdown is how much the account has dropped from a previous high point.

## What is XAUUSD?
XAUUSD is gold priced against the US dollar.

## What is MT5?
MT5, or MetaTrader 5, is the app/platform used to view charts and manage trades.

## What is Vantage?
Vantage is a broker/platform provider that can connect with MT5. Always check official terms and risk warnings.

## What is MarketVox?
MarketVox is treated as a platform/service used in the setup process. This bot can explain basic education only.
